{"type":"new","contents":"import Mathlib.Analysis.InnerProductSpace.Basic\nimport Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.GeneralLinearGroup.Basic\nimport Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.ToLin\nimport Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Determinant.Basic\nimport Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.UnitaryGroup\n\n/-!\n# Gauge Group Definitions: SU(N), PSU(N)\n\nMathlib-rooted finite matrix group definitions used by the finite Yang--Mills\nscaffold.  This file deliberately avoids carrying group laws or quotient laws as\nstructure fields: `SUN` is mathlib's special unitary matrix group, and the\ncurrent `PSUN` surface carries an explicit SU representative without asserting a\nquotient construction.\n-/\n\nnamespace InfoGeometry.Canonical.GaugeGroups\n\nopen scoped Matrix\n\nvariable {n : ℕ}\n\n/-- The special unitary group `SU(n)` as mathlib's matrix subgroup. -/\nabbrev SUN (n : ℕ) : Type :=\n  Matrix.specialUnitaryGroup (Fin n) ℂ\n\n/-- The scalar roots of unity used as the finite center data for `SU(n)`. -/\nabbrev SUNCenter (n : ℕ) : Type :=\n  { z : ℂ // z ^ n = 1 }\n\n/-- Coercion of an `SU(n)` element to its matrix representative. -/\nabbrev SUN.toMatrix (g : SUN n) : Matrix (Fin n) (Fin n) ℂ :=\n  (g : Matrix (Fin n) (Fin n) ℂ)\n\n/-- Membership readback: an `SU(n)` element is unitary and has determinant one. -/\ntheorem SUN.mem_specialUnitaryGroup (g : SUN n) :\n    g.toMatrix ∈ Matrix.specialUnitaryGroup (Fin n) ℂ :=\n  g.property\n\n/-- Unitary readback for an `SU(n)` element. -/\ntheorem SUN.is_unitary (g : SUN n) :\n    g.toMatrix ∈ Matrix.unitaryGroup (Fin n) ℂ :=\n  (Matrix.mem_specialUnitaryGroup_iff.mp g.property).1\n\n/-- Determinant-one readback for an `SU(n)` element. -/\ntheorem SUN.is_special (g : SUN n) :\n    Matrix.det g.toMatrix = 1 :=\n  (Matrix.mem_specialUnitaryGroup_iff.mp g.property).2\n\n/-- Root-of-unity readback for a center scalar. -/\ntheorem SUNCenter.pow_eq_one (z : SUNCenter n) :\n    (z : ℂ) ^ n = 1 :=\n  z.property\n\n/--\nA conservative projective-unitary surface for the current finite scaffold.\n\nIt carries a representative in `SU(n)` and does not assert that the quotient by\nscalar roots has been constructed.  Any future quotient theorem should replace\nthis abbreviation by a mathlib-rooted quotient together with proved projection\nand fiber lemmas.\n-/\nabbrev PSUN (n : ℕ) (_G : SUN n) : Type :=\n  SUN n\n\n/-- The representative matrix carried by the current conservative `PSUN` surface. -/\nabbrev PSUN.toMatrix {G : SUN n} (g : PSUN n G) : Matrix (Fin n) (Fin n) ℂ :=\n  SUN.toMatrix g\n\nend InfoGeometry.Canonical.GaugeGroups\n","mtime":1778317768345}